{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-11-13 16:49:47 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-13 23:49:47 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n\nThe durable-store and live-compilation pilots pass, but the **corpus record and companion file remain incomplete**.\n\nThe file-backed test closes and reopens the store and retrieves byte-identical evidence, a synthetic recipe, and a synthetic record. A separate live `:beta-eq-false` pilot retains its admission coordinates, input, row closure, and C1 metadata, then reproduces its root after reopening.\n\nThat pilot exposed a reconstruction issue: Jing-decoded maps compare equal to the originals, but their iteration order can differ, and the compiler uses that order when lowering dynamic maps. Capturing the observed program as EDN text reproduced the root for this fixture; it is not yet a proven corpus-wide input contract. The corpus recipe, retained dependency and expansion closure, fixture-scoped associations, and durable store location still need to be pinned before writing the companion.\n\nThe correspondence and call-site battery passed **47 tests, 614 assertions**; the two focused static oracle tests passed, and clj-kondo reported no errors or warnings. The frozen v1 table remains unchanged. No tagged run or commit was made.\n\nThe [r3 findings](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-d1/collab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-correspondence-r3.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md) are in the worktree and have not been promoted to canonical collab."}}
